<distributor xmlns=""><distorCont xmlns=""><rpIndName>Mimi D'Iorio</rpIndName><rpOrgName>Department of Commerce (DOC), National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA), Ocean and Coastal Resource Management (OCRM), National Marine Protected Areas Center (MPAC)</rpOrgName><rpPosName>GIS and Database Manager</rpPosName><rpCntInfo xmlns=""><cntPhone><voiceNum tddtty="">(831)647-6462</voiceNum><faxNum>(831)242-2051</faxNum></cntPhone><cntAddress addressType="both"><delPoint>Suite 100-F</delPoint><delPoint>99 Pacific St.</delPoint><city>Monterey</city><adminArea>CA</adminArea><postCode>93940</postCode><country>U.S.A.</country><eMailAdd>Mimi.Diorio@noaa.gov</eMailAdd></cntAddress></rpCntInfo><role><RoleCd value="005"/></role></distorCont></distributor><distFormat xmlns=""><formatName Sync="TRUE">Shapefile</formatName><formatVer>ArcGIS 10.0</formatVer></distFormat><distTranOps><transSize Sync="TRUE">0.000</transSize></distTranOps></distInfo><dataIdInfo><idCitation xmlns=""><resTitle Sync="FALSE">STEER Coastal Uses Data</resTitle><date><pubDate>2012-10-01T00:00:00</pubDate></date><citRespParty xmlns=""><rpOrgName>Department of Commerce (DOC), National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA), Ocean and Coastal Resource Management (OCRM), National Marine Protected Areas Center (MPAC)</rpOrgName><role><RoleCd value="006"/></role></citRespParty><presForm xmlns=""><PresFormCd value="005"/></presForm><presForm xmlns=""><fgdcGeoform>vector digital data</fgdcGeoform></presForm></idCitation><idAbs>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;The Coastal Use Mapping Project is designed to collect critical information on human activities in and near the St. Thomas East End Reserves (STEER). The project purpose is to improve understanding of the spatial range and intensity of key human activities and uses in this region in order to better inform resource management. Workshops were held on St. Thomas where the public, scientists, and stakeholders were invited to participate in creating maps of ocean uses for the STEER.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</idAbs><idPurp>Coral reefs in the USVI are facing increasing pressures from a growing variety of ocean uses, as well as increased coastal development and watershed impacts. The STEER contains extensive mangroves, seagrass beds and coral reefs. It houses a variety of commercial activities and is adjacent to a landfill, marinas, an EPA Superfund Site, and residential areas served by individual septic systems. The Coastal Use Mapping Project is intended as a step to improving coastal and watershed management activities. The information collected through this project will provide a better understanding of human uses, issues, and constraints in the STEER. It can help inform management decisions to better protect the ecosystem, while minimizing impacts on those who depend on marine resources and reducing user conflict. The project includes collecting and mapping existing watershed information, and conducting participatory mapping workshops to gain a better understanding of key human uses and use motivations that affect the STEER.</idPurp><idStatus><ProgCd value="001"/></idStatus><idPoC xmlns=""><rpIndName>Mimi D'Iorio</rpIndName><rpOrgName>Department of Commerce (DOC), National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA), Ocean and Coastal Resource Management (OCRM), National Marine Protected Areas Center (MPAC)</rpOrgName><rpPosName>GIS and Database Manager</rpPosName><rpCntInfo xmlns=""><cntPhone><voiceNum tddtty="">(831)647-6462 x112</voiceNum><faxNum>(831)242-2051</faxNum></cntPhone><cntAddress addressType="both"><delPoint>99 Pacific St. Suite 100-F</delPoint><city>Monterey</city><adminArea>CA</adminArea><postCode>93940</postCode><country>U.S.A.</country><eMailAdd>Mimi.Diorio@noaa.gov</eMailAdd></cntAddress></rpCntInfo><role><RoleCd value="007"/></role></idPoC><resMaint xmlns=""><maintFreq><MaintFreqCd value="009"/></maintFreq><maintCont xmlns=""><rpIndName>Jordan Gass</rpIndName><rpOrgName>Department of Commerce (DOC), National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA), Ocean and Coastal Resource Management (OCRM), National Marine Protected Areas Center (MPAC)</rpOrgName><rpPosName>GIS Specialist</rpPosName><rpCntInfo xmlns=""><cntPhone><voiceNum tddtty="">(831)647-1920</voiceNum><faxNum>(831)647-1732</faxNum></cntPhone><cntAddress addressType="both"><delPoint>Suite 100-F</delPoint><delPoint>99 Pacific St.</delPoint><city>Monterey</city><adminArea>CA</adminArea><postCode>93940</postCode><country>U.S.A.</country><eMailAdd>Jordan.Gass@noaa.gov</eMailAdd></cntAddress></rpCntInfo><role><RoleCd value="007"/></role><displayName>Jordan Gass</displayName><displayName>Jordan Gass</displayName></maintCont></resMaint><placeKeys xmlns=""><keyword>STEER</keyword><keyword>Caribbean</keyword><keyword>St. Thomas</keyword><keyword>U.S. Virgin Islands</keyword></placeKeys><themeKeys xmlns=""><thesaName><resTitle>ISO 19115 Topic Category</resTitle></thesaName><keyword>geoscientificInformation</keyword><keyword>society</keyword><keyword>oceans</keyword><keyword>environment</keyword></themeKeys><themeKeys xmlns=""><keyword>Whelk fishing</keyword><keyword>Charter boat tours</keyword><keyword>Mooring</keyword><keyword>Ferry transit</keyword><keyword>Thrill Craft</keyword><keyword>SCUBA</keyword><keyword>Fishing</keyword><keyword>Paddling</keyword><keyword>Spearfishing</keyword><keyword>Water Sports</keyword><keyword>Charter Snorkeling</keyword><keyword>Handline fishing</keyword><keyword>SNUBA</keyword><keyword>Shore Fishing</keyword><keyword>Transient mooring</keyword><keyword>Swimming</keyword><keyword>Recreational Dive Fishing</keyword><keyword>Sailing</keyword><keyword>Camping</keyword><keyword>Recreational Harvest</keyword><keyword>Ocean Uses</keyword><keyword>Snorkeling</keyword><keyword>Research</keyword><keyword>Non-Extractive Use</keyword><keyword>Wildlife Viewing</keyword><keyword>Anchoring</keyword